questions.questionText:
A 'C' program is written to take three integers with different values as an input and identify the largest number amongst them.
Write the missing code in the given box to achieve the mentioned task.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main( )
{
  int n1, n2, n3;
  printf("Enter three different numbers: \n");
  scanf("%d %d %d", &n1, &n2, &n3);

  /* Write missing conditional logic here */

  return 0;
}
```

questions.modelAnswer:
**Missing Conditional Code (C Language):**
```c
if ((n1 > n2) && (n1 > n3))
{
    printf("%d is the largest", n1);
}
else if ((n2 > n1) && (n2 > n3))
{
    printf("%d is the largest", n2);
}
else
{
    printf("%d is the largest", n3);
}
```

**2025 Syllabus Equivalent (JavaScript):**
```javascript
if ((n1 > n2) && (n1 > n3)) {
    document.write(n1 + " is the largest");
} else if ((n2 > n1) && (n2 > n3)) {
    document.write(n2 + " is the largest");
} else {
    document.write(n3 + " is the largest");
}
```

questions.questionText:
Convert the following `for` loop into `do-while` loop.

```c
for (int i=20;i<50;i+=5)
printf("\n%d", i);
```

questions.modelAnswer:
**Converted `do-while` Loop (C Language):**
```c
int i = 20;
do
{
    printf("\n%d", i);
    i += 5;
}
while (i < 50);
```

**2025 Syllabus Equivalent (JavaScript):**
```javascript
let i = 20;
do {
    document.write(i + "<br>");
    i += 5;
} while (i < 50);
```

### Option (a): Multiplication Table up to Inputted Range Using `while` Loop

**C Program:**
```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main()
{
    int num, range, i = 1, result;
    printf("Enter a number for table: ");
    scanf("%d", &num);
    printf("Enter range of the table: ");
    scanf("%d", &range);
    while (i <= range)
    {
        result = num * i;
        printf("%d * %d = %d\n", num, i, result);
        i = i + 1;
    }
    return 0;
}
```

**2025 Syllabus JavaScript Equivalent:**
```javascript
let num = Number(prompt("Enter a number for table:"));
let range = Number(prompt("Enter range of the table:"));
let i = 1;
while (i <= range) {
    let result = num * i;
    document.write(num + " * " + i + " = " + result + "<br>");
    i++;
}
```

### Option (b): Check Whether an Input Character is a Vowel or a Consonant

**C Program:**
```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main()
{
    char ch;
    printf("Enter an alphabet: ");
    scanf(" %c", &ch);
    if ((ch >= 'A' && ch <= 'Z') || (ch >= 'a' && ch <= 'z'))
    {
        if (ch == 'a' || ch == 'e' || ch == 'i' || ch == 'o' || ch == 'u' ||
            ch == 'A' || ch == 'E' || ch == 'I' || ch == 'O' || ch == 'U')
        {
            printf("%c is a vowel", ch);
        }
        else
        {
            printf("%c is a consonant", ch);
        }
    }
    else
    {
        printf("Invalid character");
    }
    return 0;
}
```

